So I think this one's OK.  As you can see, the state
transitions are well estimated, but the locations of
the von Mises have fairly broad posteriors, which makes
sense given their wide scales.

It would be even better to fit this model with proper
circular parameters.  I'll need to figure out how to
do that with our unit_vector parameter type, but I
should be able to get that done for a case study (a
unit_vector[2] will provide a point on a circle which
can then be translated back to an angle---all this trig
makes my head hurt).

When I get some time write the case study out, I'll also
show how to pull out the best predicted path of states
(use the Viterbi algorithm) and the marginals over states
at each point in time (that requires full forward-backward).
