Larry's tutorial's a classic---I saw him present it more
than once at Bell Labs when I used to work in natural language
and speech recognition.  Bishop's machine learning book is
nice and it contains the generalized algorithms and approximations,
as is Durbin's book on biological sequences.  I imagine
the Langrock et al. HMM book is good---I like their doc for
moveHMM.

- Bob

