While awaiting your full/commented code, thought I'd send one speed-up idea: If you have an equal number of observations at each zip location, store them in a NxM matrix where N is the number of zips and M is the number of observations per zip. Then the distance matrix is just NxN and you can loop over the M observations using that same distance matrix.

