Hmm... I don't trust timing on a cluster without knowing the intrinsic variance between runs. I don't trust timing numbers on even a single machine. Just a statement of fact: we run some timing tests on a single machine, Mac Pro. We get differences of 2x in total time depending on what's happening on the machine. That's on one machine that is sitting on my desk. I don't know about how stable timing numbers are across different cluster nodes or if something else messes with IO.

