>   rho   0.27       0 0.09 0.14  0.49  24539    1
>   > mean(rowSums(get_elapsed_time(post3)))/60
>   [1] 29.12736
>   > sd(rowSums(get_elapsed_time(post3)))/60
>   [1] 0.3682616
>
> Admittedly, 30%ish isn't a huge performance difference, but I was surprised to see any difference this consistent at all.

30% is huge. I wouldn't expect that.

First, are the computations identical? All of the draws should have the same exact values. If not, there's a coding difference.

Do you see this locally? What about with CmdStan? Have you replicated the same seed multiple times for timing? (Maybe one chain with the seed, as opposed to timing across multiple chains).

30% isn't good. I wonder if it's possibly IO related.

Could you stan_rdump() the data and kick out the 2 Stan programs and I'll try to run it at the office?

