From uda33143a8db60ce8 at groups.google.com  Sun Sep 11 00:52:51 2016
From: uda33143a8db60ce8 at groups.google.com (Andrew Gelman)
Date: Sun, 11 Sep 2016 00:52:51 +0000
Subject: why tau, not tausq
Message-ID: <JwmsztFcqWM.WB5De-GoAgAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <JwmsztFcqWM.7XtEM5CoAgAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <JwmsztFcqWM.NGYh7HWaAgAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com> <JwmsztFcqWM.7XtEM5CoAgAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/JwmsztFcqWM/m/WB5De-GoAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1.  Inv-gamma has problems (see Gelman, 2006).
2.  tau is more interpretable than tausq.  You can have prior info on tau, it's not so clear how to do that with tausq
3.  Normal dist in Stan uses the normal(mean, sd) parameterization, NOT normal(mean, var).
That pretty much covers it!

