>  18: SEXP fileabc6684483e( SEXP x, SEXP y ){
>  19: return ScalarReal( INTEGER(x)[0] * REAL(y)[0] )
>  20: Rf_warning("your C++ program does not return anything");
>  21:  return R_NilValue ;
>  22: }

For some reason, your R code yields a C++ function that is missing the terminating semi-colon on line 19. Are you sure you pasted in exactly

fx <- inline::cxxfunction( signature(x = "integer", y = "numeric" ) , '

    return ScalarReal( INTEGER(x)[0] * REAL(y)[0] ) ;
' )
fx( 2L, 5 ) # should be 10

Otherwise, I don't know why it would do that. Maybe try reinstalling Rcpp. Or it could be something with the language settings on your computer.

Ben

