On Wednesday, September 14, 2016 at 11:18:25 PM UTC-4, ralphe...@gmail.com wrote:
> So in my actual problem, I'm trying to fit a surface with a parametric curve (e.g. polynomial) with parameters that are time-varying random walks, so it would be more like:
>
> parameters{
> real a[T];
> real b[T];
> ...
> real sigma;
> }
>
> model{
> ...
> for (t in 2:T)
>          a[t] ~ normal(a[t-1],sigma_a);
>          b[t] ~ normal(b[t-1],sigma_b);
>          x[t] ~ normal(a[t]*xvals^2 + b[t]*xvals^3 + ....., sigma); //This is not a valid line of code
> ...
> }
>
