You can rewrite this

       if ( cens[i] ==0 ) {
            log_lik[i] = -log(sqrt(2*pi())) - log(sigma) - (diff[i])^2/2;}
        else if ( cens[i] ==1 ) {
            log_lik[i] = normal_lcdf(diff[i] | 0, 1);}

more efficiently as:

  log_lik[i] = cens[i] ? normal_lcdf(diff[i] | 0, 1) : normal_lpdf(diff[i] | 0, sigma);

But shouldn't that normal_lcdf also have sigma instead of 1 so they
match?

- Bob

> On Sep 15, 2016, at 6:28 PM, Thao Tran <thao...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Hi Seth,
> Thanks for your input.
> Actually I meant the loglikelihood that genearted by the generated quantities in Stan.
> My model is as below:
> model_ex0 <- "
> data {
>      int<lower=1> N;                         // Total number of data points
