Hi Bob,

I read the section 18 on custom probability functions, as you suggested.

I wrote a function called radius_lpdf (below, along the lines of the one supplied by Daniel Rosenbluth).
It interpolates a sample at a given radius from log10(pdf) which is given by a lookup table.

When I included radius_lpdf in the function block, it compiled successfully.

But when I tried to sample from it with the ~ notation in the model block, Stan threw an error, saying the function didn't exist;
See below:

model {

    // Hyperpriors
    alpha ~ uniform(-10,5);
    beta ~ uniform(-5,5);
    lnf0 ~ uniform(-5,5);
    xthis ~ uniform(-.5,4)

    for (n in 1:nKois)
        koi_rps_true[n] ~ radius_lpdf(lookup_tbl[n], nrow_lkup_tbl, x_lo, x_hi, x_linstep, x_this);

    // Sample using lnLikelihood function
    increment_log_prob(lnlike(alpha, beta, lnf0, nKois, planet_radius_rng, x_rng, vol, x_grid, planet_radius_grid, koi_x, koi_rps_true, nRadiusGrid, nxGrid, e, new_completeness));
}

Stan's error message:

No matches for:

  real ~ radius_lpdf(real[], int, real, real, real, real)

Distribution radius_lpdf not found.

ERROR at line 290

 289:        for (n in 1:nKois)
 290:            koi_rps_true[n] ~ radius_lpdf(lookup_tbl[n], nrow_lkup_tbl, x_lo, x_hi, x_linstep, x_this);

What am I doing wrong?

Thanks!

Joe

// This function does linear interpolation in a lookup table for log radius pdf
// The lookup_tbl has to be provided as data.

    real radius_lpdf(real[] lookup_tbl,

                                int nrow_lkup_tbl,
                                real x_lo,
                                real x_hi,
                                real x_linstep,

                                real x_this) {
        // Outputs radius logpdf, using linear interpolation

        // lookup_tbl: Provided as data
        // nrow_lkup_tbl: # rows in lookup_tbl
        // x_lo, x_hi: Outside these bounds, use analytic formulas for tail behavior

        // x_linstep: Linear step size

        // x_this: The value to compute

        real x_a; // x-value to left of x_this in table
        int idx_a; // index of x_a in table
        real f_a; // log-prob of x_a
        real f_b; // log-prob of x_b (value to right of x_this in table)
        real perc; // Used in interpolation

        if( x_this < -365) {
            return negative_infinity(); // at -365, log-prob is -5e306
        }
        if( x_this < x_lo ) {

            return negative_infinity(); // left tail behavior
        }
        if (x_this > x_hi) {
            return  negative_infinity(); // right tail behavior

        }

        // Linear interpolation
        idx_a <- 1 + as_integer_bsearch( (x_this - x_lo)/x_linstep, nrow_lkup_tbl);
        x_a   <- x_lo + x_linstep * (idx_a - 1);
        perc <- (x_this - x_a)/x_linstep;

        f_a <- lookup_tbl[idx_a];
        f_b <- lookup_tbl[idx_a+1];

        return f_a  + (f_b - f_a) * perc;
    }

