Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/SPlQPDH6f6U/m/Q2eZi87qBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I'll try this out tomorrow, but I think I can solve my sampling problem by using a MVN approximation to logits.

Using logits rather than raw probabilities is easy enough when using 2 groups, but harder with > 2 groups.
If dirichlet, like beta, can't be sampled well due to probability near constraints (and thus, basically, walls), I wonder if I can:
Use softmax regression to estimate logits of groups, then place a MVN(logits[n], 5*1.6*Identity) prior on that as an approximation to a dirichlet.

That is, rather than using: pi[n,1:K] ~ dirichlet(somePredicted/Hierarchical parameters), I could use pi_logit[n,1:K] ~ multinormal(somePredicted/Hierarchical parameters, scaling to adjust multinormal akin to using N(0,1.6) as logistic approx).

I'll play with this tomorrow.

